 ### Sphere Impostors for DEM Pebbles
-Sphere Impostors for DEM Pebbles renders Discrete Element Method (DEM) pebble beds using instanced sphere impostors. Each pebble is drawn as a quad with an exact orthographic ray-sphere hit test in the fragment shader, providing sphere shading and depth. It draws DEM centres, not solver geometry, and renders to an offscreen target for interaction while positions stream. It scales to 27,000 pebbles at interactive rates with 1.2-1.3 ms of CPU overhead per frame. If no wgpu device is available, egui discs are used as the fallback rendering method [S2, unofficial].
