 ### Splat quad vertex layout
-Splat quad vertex layout sets up a 4-vertex quad with specific coordinates for shader-based scaling of projected 2D Gaussian eigenvectors. Vertex positions are defined as $(-2,-2), (2,-2), (2,2), (-2,2)$. Indices are $0,1,2,0,2,3$. The vertex buffer uses `VET_FLOAT2` at `VES_POSITION`. The index buffer uses `IT_16BIT`. The instance buffer contains 1 float per instance (`VET_FLOAT1`, `VES_TEXTURE_COORDINATES[0]`, location 8) [S3, unofficial].
