 ### Uniform Object Distribution via Modulo Instancing
-Uniform Object Distribution via Modulo Instancing is a technique where a modulo function is applied to the scene distance function to repeat a single SDF component with a defined interval, generating a uniform grid of object copies. A pitfall is that cutting off the previous grid hit by a ray may result in 3D objects associated with the cell and potentially intersected by the ray being removed from the scene. The original single-pass approach causes visible artifacts from many vantage points despite using Existence operators to reduce visibility [S4].
